  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-10-09T00:52:33.311Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The new UI feels very counter-intuitive towards people with disabities. I resuggest that you use a much more visual/icon system or an optional feature for this so that users who struggle to read amongst other disabilities are able to play the game.\nI suggest the menu has more streamlined options. A more linear approach if you will. I feel like there's no need for three different selections to be able to reach the same destination. The compartmentalization seems rather unnecessary. Perhaps an 'advanced mode'(?)\nFinally, I know nobody likes criticism on these things, but I feel like it's quite essential to make it more welcoming towards new users. I'm a trusted user and I felt rather confused on certain things leading me in the same direction, like I said, a more linear approach would be much more appreciated than all the optional things all over the place, this also comes back to confusion towards people who might have disabilities and may struggle to use these features properly.\nI know that people might feel like \"you'll get used to it\", but I also feel like this should be considered as first impressions can be very tangant towards approaching newer users, and in all, it feels too complicated.\nI hope you can consider this feedback towards a newer build of the game.",
